      obj: ['O‘tgan voqealarni muntazam fe’llarning o‘tgan zamon shakli (-ed) bilan aytasiz.', 'You will talk about finished events with the Past Simple of regular verbs (-ed).'],
      ex: ['Past Simple tugagan o‘tgan voqealar uchun: I visited my aunt yesterday. Muntazam fe’llarga -ed qo‘shiladi: work → worked. -e bilan tugasa faqat -d: live → lived. Undosh + y → -ied: study → studied. Qisqa unli + undosh juftlanadi: stop → stopped.\n-ed uch xil talaffuz qilinadi: /t/ (worked), /d/ (played), /ɪd/ (wanted, needed). Vaqt so‘zlari: yesterday, last week, two days ago.', 'The Past Simple describes finished events: I visited my aunt yesterday. Regular verbs add -ed: work → worked; -e verbs add -d: live → lived; consonant + y becomes -ied: study → studied; a short vowel + consonant doubles: stop → stopped.\n-ed is pronounced /t/ (worked), /d/ (played) or /ɪd/ (wanted). Time words: yesterday, last week, two days ago.'],
      eg: [['Yesterday I visited my grandmother.', 'Kecha buvimnikiga bordim.'], ['She studied English last year.', 'U o‘tgan yili ingliz tilini o‘rgandi.'], ['We stopped at the shop.', 'Biz do‘konda to‘xtadik.'], ['They watched a film two days ago.', 'Ular ikki kun oldin film ko‘rishdi.']],
      w: [['yesterday', 'kecha', 'вчера', 'adverb', 'I called my mother yesterday.', 'Kecha onamga qo‘ng‘iroq qildim.', 'ˈjestədeɪ'], ['ago', 'avval, oldin', 'назад', 'adverb', 'He arrived two hours ago.', 'U ikki soat oldin yetib keldi.', 'əˈɡəʊ'], ['last week', 'o‘tgan hafta', 'на прошлой неделе', 'phrase', 'We moved here last week.', 'Biz bu yerga o‘tgan hafta ko‘chib keldik.', 'ˌlɑːst ˈwiːk'], ['then', 'keyin', 'потом', 'adverb', 'We ate and then we walked.', 'Biz ovqatlandik, keyin sayr qildik.', 'ðen'], ['after that', 'shundan keyin', 'после этого', 'phrase', 'After that we went home.', 'Shundan keyin uyga ketdik.', 'ˌɑːftə ˈðæt'], ['finally', 'nihoyat', 'наконец', 'adverb', 'Finally the bus arrived.', 'Nihoyat avtobus keldi.', 'ˈfaɪnəli']],
